    summary_en: "The industry-standard workstation graphics benchmark, SPECViewPerf 15.0.1, has officially released its Linux version. This version represents a major upgrade from the previous Linux version, SPECViewPerf 2020. SPECViewPerf 15.0.1 supports x86_64 and AArch64 architectures for workstations. While the Windows version incorporates DirectX 12 and Vulkan support, the Linux version currently supports only OpenGL 4.5. This tool allows users to evaluate and compare the performance of different workstation GPUs and drivers, making it valuable for hardware testing and performance benchmarking. Users can find more information at SPEC.org.",
