    summary_en: "Apple is bringing several major upgrades to Apple Pay in iOS 27, enhancing the user payment experience. Key updates include a redesigned checkout interface, allowing users to switch between different cards and view card rewards and balances more easily. Furthermore, Apple has partnered with American Express, enabling users to directly use Membership Rewards points to offset part or all of the purchase amount during the Apple Pay checkout process. Another new feature, 'Tap to Share,' integrates with Apple Pay, making physical store shopping more convenient. Users can now securely share information such as emails, addresses, and membership points with a simple tap, and view their shopping cart contents in real-time. Additionally, users can manage the balance of their signed-in card and directly add funds to the card within the Apple Pay interface. On the retail side, Walmart has begun rolling out Apple Pay support in Arkansas and plans to cover all its US stores by the end of the year.",
