    summary_en: "Apple has introduced a major update to the Photos app in iOS 27, adding a dedicated feature called 'Captured by Me.' This feature aims to address the previous lack of a pure display space for user-shot content within the Photos app. Unlike the current 'Recents' album, which contains a mix of shared content, memories, and screenshots, 'Captured by Me' specifically collects and displays all photos and videos taken using the Camera app. It excludes other types of content, such as images sent by friends or screenshots. This update allows users to view their original self-shot media more precisely, enhancing the overall photo management experience. Users can access this feature through the new 'Captured by Me' album or by using a filter in the main library.",
