    summary_en: "According to the article, when Apple released the M4 Mac mini, its internal SSD was not soldered to the motherboard, which allowed users to perform third-party storage upgrades. However, the article points out that with the updates for the next-generation M6 and M5 Pro Mac mini, rumors suggest that the storage may once again be soldered onto the motherboard. This means that future users may no longer be able to upgrade the machine's storage capacity by replacing the SSD themselves, as was possible in the past. This represents a significant design change for users who value customization and repair flexibility, potentially impacting the future upgrade maintenance costs and convenience of the Mac mini.",
