    summary_en: "Qualcomm today announced two flagship chips: the Snapdragon 8 Elite Gen 6 and the Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6, designed for next-generation Android smartphones. Both chips utilize a 2nm process, featuring an Oryon CPU core configuration that includes two 5GHz Prime Cores and six 4GHz Performance cores. Compared to the previous Gen 5, the Elite Gen 6 offers a 10% boost in CPU performance and a 37% improvement in power efficiency. The Elite Extreme Gen 6 boosts CPU performance by 13% and includes a global VVC (H.266) decoder to enhance energy efficiency. Furthermore, the redesigned Adreno GPU improves performance by 35% and energy efficiency by 40%. The Extreme Gen 6 further integrates dedicated AI Adreno matrix cores, boosting GPU performance by 44% and providing 18 MB of high-performance memory. The Hexagon NPU features a new Element Accelerator optimized for Transformer workloads, achieving a 14% performance increase. The most notable feature of the Extreme Gen 6 is its support for 30B+ parameter MoE models and the inclusion of the X105 5G Modem, which supports 3GPP Release 19 5G Advanced. These advancements aim to enhance AI computing, image processing (such as 8K60 video recording), and connectivity capabilities.",
